    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1110">

                <pb facs="0928" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4025.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-25T10:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1912—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Zapata’s communication mentioned in my May 24, 5 p.m., has been addressed to all
                    consuls general here and the evening papers have published its substance; I
                    learned this after sending my telegram. Perfect arrangements for concentration
                    of American colony have for some time been in effect. Consul General made no
                    reply to Zapata, whose letter caused but little alarm here; it is believed his
                    forces are insufficiently armed to undertake a considerable movement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
